  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following elements have half-filled f-orbitals in their ground state ?<br />(Given : atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sm</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>Eu</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>Tb</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>Gd</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Pm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>61</mn></math>)</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A and B only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C and D only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "B and D only",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "A and E only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>f-subshell contains seven orbitals in it. Hence, if seven electrons are present in these&nbsp;orbitals then it said to be half-filled. Electronic&nbsp;configuration of all the elements are:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sm</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Eu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Tb</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Gd</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Pm</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>61</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Eu</mi></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Gd</mi></math> have half-filled configuration.</p>"
  }
